title: Paying for the Revolution
card-image: img/cards/finance.svg?v=2
subtitle: The ruble, the Liberty Loan and the printing press.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: coalition_affairs
view-if: finance_timer <= 0 and bol_regime = 0 and dix >= 4
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; finance_timer = 3

The war costs forty million rubles a day, and the Treasury covers most of it with the printing press. Prices in Petrograd have trebled since February; the peasants will not sell grain for paper. (The ruble: [+ ruble : ruble +].)

- @loan: Campaign for the Liberty Loan. (1 resource)
- @tax: Demand a tax on war profits and the great fortunes.
- @austerity: Cut the state's spending, and the army's.
- @print: Let the Treasury print, and feed the cities with it.
- @easy_discard

@loan
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We cannot afford the campaign.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
RO.add(Q, {ruble: 4, rel_kad: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {middle: 2});
!}

The party's speakers sold the Liberty Loan in the factories and the barracks as a loan to the revolution. Some of it was even bought by people who could not afford it.

@tax

How should the party go about it? Cautiously, with compromises, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. In full, it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can carry it out and break its opponents.

- @tax_slow: Go about it cautiously, with compromises.
- @tax_decree: Carry it out in full.
- @tax_force: Carry it out in full, and break any opposition by force.

@tax_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.add(Q, {ruble: 6, rel_kad: -5, right_threat: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, middle: -3});
}, "Demand a tax on war profits and the great fortunes");
!}

The excess-profits tax was carried, and the great fortunes were assessed. The Moscow industrialists say that they will close their factories first; the ruble has steadied for the first time since the spring. (It was done cautiously, with compromises.)



@tax_decree
subtitle: All that it says. Its opponents will answer.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'decree', () => {
RO.add(Q, {ruble: 6, rel_kad: -5, right_threat: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, middle: -3});
}, "Demand a tax on war profits and the great fortunes");
!}

The excess-profits tax was carried, and the great fortunes were assessed. The Moscow industrialists say that they will close their factories first; the ruble has steadied for the first time since the spring.



@tax_force
view-if: bol_regime = 0
choose-if: strength >= 18
subtitle: Your chance of breaking each camp it angers: Kadets [+ odds_kad +]%, generals [+ odds_gen +]%. Any camp under 45% is too strong for you, and is left alone.
unavailable-subtitle: We lack the force and the allies to break the opposition.
on-arrival: {!

RO.law(Q, 'force', () => {
RO.add(Q, {ruble: 6, rel_kad: -5, right_threat: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 3, middle: -3});
}, "Demand a tax on war profits and the great fortunes");
!}

The excess-profits tax was carried, and the great fortunes were assessed. The Moscow industrialists say that they will close their factories first; the ruble has steadied for the first time since the spring. [+ law_text +]

@austerity
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {ruble: 5, army_discipline: -3, war_weariness: 1, bread: -1});
RO.boost(Q, {bureaucrats: -2, soldiers: -2});
!}

The ministries were told to cut, and the army's quartermasters with them. The ruble is a little firmer; the officers and the officials are not happy, and neither are the men who are owed their pay.

@print
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {ruble: -3, bread: 3});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 1});
!}

The presses ran through the night, and the cities were fed for another month. Everyone knows what it costs, and that the bill is paid later.
